# RobOS — Windsurf Rules

## What Is RobOS

RobOS is a Linux-based desktop OS (Ubuntu + GNOME) purpose-built for software engineers. Every virtual desktop maps to a Jira ticket. MCP servers connect an AI layer to GitHub, Jira, Slack, VPNs, IDEs, calendars, and the desktop itself. GUI apps are Electron-based and live in `packages/<app-id>/`.

---

## Development Workflow — Harness First, VM Second

**Never use SSH deploy as the primary testing strategy.**

1. Iterate using the dev harness sandbox:
   ```bash
   node packages/dev-harness/harness.js --app <app-id> --scenario <scenario>
   node packages/dev-harness/harness.js --list-apps
   node packages/dev-harness/harness.js --list-scenarios
   ```
   Scenarios: `all-good`, `no-gh-auth`, `no-ssh-key`, `ssh-not-on-github`, `scope-missing`, `git-config-missing`, `all-broken`

2. Only deploy to VM after harness confirms end-to-end success:
   ```bash
   ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no -p 2224 robos@localhost
   packages/desktop-shell/install.sh   # run inside VM
   ```

VM launch: `./infra/desktop/run.sh` (`--vnc` for VNC display at `vncviewer localhost:5910`)

